<title>NORWAY: Kvaerner signs 3 deals worth 450 mln NOK.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner signs 3 deals worth 450 mln NOK.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian industrial group Kvaerner ASA said on Monday it had recently signed three construction contracts in Tampa, Florida, worth more than 450 million crowns altogether.  </p>
<p>Kvaerner said in a statement to the Oslo Bourse the contracts had been won by Kvaerner Construction Inc., which is based in Tampa.</p>
<p>One contract worth 190 million crowns is for the construction of a school in Sun City, another 190 million crown deal is for rebuilding a school in Orlando and the third contract, worth more than 70 million crowns, involves adding a section at the University of Central Florida.</p>
<p>--Rolf Soderlind, Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
